<title>USA: Florida citrus belt hot and dry again - FASS.</title>
<headline>Florida citrus belt hot and dry again - FASS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>This was another hot and dry week in Florida's citrus belt, the Florida Agricultural Statistics Service (FASS), said.</p>
<p>In its weekly weather and crop update, FASS said there was very good condition in most well-cared for groves. Recent new growth has hardened and trees generally appear dark green, according to FASS. New crop fruit continues to make good progress with shedding of excessive little green fruit almost complete.</p>
<p>Growers and caretakers have been irrigating around the clock to maintain good tree condition, FASS said.</p>
<p>FASS reported an estimated 6,073,000 boxes of Valencia oranges were harvested in the week ended May 18, down from 8,028,000 in the prior week and compared with 7,727,000 during the week ended May 4.</p>
<p>((-- New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
